==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[ethical]] [[dative]]|-}}

# {{grammar}} a form of the [[dative case]] applied to [[pronoun]]s; used (in [[Latin]] and some other languages, but rare in [[English]]) to show a certain interest felt by the person indicated
#: Examples. 
:"Knock ''me'' on this door."
:"Get ''you'' home!"
:"Hie ''thee'' hence."
:"Get ''thee'' behind me, Satan!"
:"I'll rhyme ''you'' so eight years together," - Shakespeare, ''As You Like It'', 3.2
:"Get ''thee'' to a nunnery." - Shakespeare, ''Hamlet'', 3.1
:"Knock ''me'' at this gate." - Shakespeare, ''Taming of the Shrew'', 1.2


